>> title: Chicken Pesto Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: chicken, farro, pesto, parmesan, skillet, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: chicken pesto bowl, pesto chicken bowl, chicken pesto parm, pesto grain bowl, farro bowl, grain bowl, power bowl
>> pairs-with: basil-pesto
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min

>> step: The frico is the point: parmesan dropped on a dry pan and left until it stops bubbling lifts off as a crisp sheet.
The frico is the point.

>> step: boil 25 min, drain
Boil @pearled farro{1 1/4%cups}(230 g) in @salted water{2%qt}(1.9 L) ~boil{25%min}, until tender but still chewy, then drain it well.

>> step: fold the pesto through hot
Fold @basil pesto{1/3%cup}(80 mL) through @&(~1)hot farro{} — warm grain takes a pesto up, cold grain only wears it.

>> step: sear 8 min, rest 5 min, slice
Sear @chicken breasts{1 1/4%lb}(570 g; halved horizontally) rubbed with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and @kosher salt{1%tsp} in a hot #skillet{} ~sear{8%min}, turning once, until it springs back, then ~rest{5%min} and slice.

>> step: blister 5 min, undisturbed
Blister @cherry tomatoes{1%pint}(280 g) in @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in the same #skillet{} ~sear{5%min}, undisturbed, until the skins split and catch on the pan.

>> step: fry 4 min, until the bubbling stops
Fry @grated Parmesan{3/4%cup}(65 g) as four thin rounds in a dry #nonstick skillet{} ~fry{4%min}, until the bubbling stops and the edges go to lace, then lift them onto a rack to ~cool{2%min}.

>> step: build it, crisps standing up
Spoon @&(~4)pesto farro{} into four bowls, lay @&(~3)sliced chicken{} and @&(~2)blistered tomatoes{} over it, add @baby spinach{3%cups}(packed), @lemon{1/2}(juiced) and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, and stand @&(~1)parmesan crisps{} up in the top.
